From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: L33TEST Crossroads <dullclarity@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] multizorkd: bind listener to loopback (::1) only

multizorkd has no CLI option for a bind address; prep_listen_socket() passes
NULL to getaddrinfo(), binding every interface. This deployment reaches the
daemon only through a co-located local relay, so bind ::1.

Network-binding change only: no gameplay, protocol, or on-disk format change.
This reconstructs the single local modification already present in the
in-production multizorkd binary (SHA-256 6dcdde18...5536fc89).
---
 multizorkd.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/multizorkd.c b/multizorkd.c
index df86a6d..c96a9f8 100644
--- a/multizorkd.c
+++ b/multizorkd.c
@@ -2454,7 +2454,10 @@ static int prep_listen_socket(const int port, const int backlog)
     hints.ai_socktype = SOCK_STREAM;
     hints.ai_flags = AI_V4MAPPED | AI_NUMERICSERV | AI_PASSIVE;    // AI_PASSIVE for the "any" address.
     snprintf(service, sizeof (service), "%u", (uint) port);
-    const int gairc = getaddrinfo(NULL, service, &hints, &ainfo);
+    // Deployment change: bind the listener to loopback only ("::1") instead of
+    //  every interface (NULL). multizorkd has no CLI flag to choose a bind
+    //  address and is only ever reached through a co-located local relay.
+    const int gairc = getaddrinfo("::1", service, &hints, &ainfo);
     if (gairc != 0) {
         loginfo("getaddrinfo() failed to find where we should bind! (%s)", gai_strerror(gairc));
         return -1;
